nswer is \"IV only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186350714 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b1bb974-826a-590f-8d32-cdc868ca827c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subspaces of Polynomial Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b35e9b78-e8d2-5093-b98a-ae292b1eee74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350716} {:answer/id #uuid "3f89fad8-0ca0-5db4-bf6f-64d3cbcef30a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350717} {:answer/id #uuid "190e2d24-933b-53c7-aae8-7ea84d0afeff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350718} {:answer/id #uuid "75d9380f-8715-5426-8789-58be8bc8554e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350719} {:answer/id #uuid "12672104-d324-5966-974b-1f7037bcb687" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350720}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "12672104-d324-5966-974b-1f7037bcb687" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350720} :answer-field/id #uuid "80e3d5f6-a690-5cd1-a2ba-5bbb36417f6c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350715}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "28aa2636-f782-5fe9-b540-5ed6dba0b402" :question/math-academy-id "q-94615" :question/problem "Consider the vector space ${R}_{4}[t]$ of all polynomials in the variable $t$ of degree at most $4,$ and its subset $B={p(t)\\in {R}_{4}[t]\\,|\\,p(0)=1}.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $B$ is closed under polynomial addition\n- $B$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n- $B$ is a subspace of ${R}_{4}[t]$\n- $B$ is **not** a subspace of ${R}_{4}[t]$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. For example, if $f(0)=g(0)=1,$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0)+g(0) & =1+1 \\\\  & =2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is not a polynomial from $B.$ So, $B$ is *not* closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is false. For example, if $f(0)=1$ and $k=2,$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}kf(0) & =1\\cdot 2=2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is not a polynomial from $B.$ So, $B$ is *not* closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is false, while statement IV is true. $B$ is *not* a subspace because it's not closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"IV only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186350721 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8f306cf2-6881-5948-90bd-4e0ce98b4116" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subspaces of Matrix Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05108eaf-4154-5697-a464-b90f33cb0dd2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350723} {:answer/id #uuid "a109718a-6c2b-532d-815f-2ce4d465b50f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350724} {:answer/id #uuid "e8937969-ed6d-59fd-9b5a-f0d84beefab2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350725} {:answer/id #uuid "62c9bad0-ac48-5c98-88e8-73c8e6c27608" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350726} {:answer/id #uuid "5b2781a3-caab-537a-82cc-c2ea05580196" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350727}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e8937969-ed6d-59fd-9b5a-f0d84beefab2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350725} :answer-field/id #uuid "f18c62f7-5f84-5dc2-a651-1bec76758a82" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350722}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d2a8d859-2d67-56f3-a406-cd87fb45d2da" :question/math-academy-id "q-94624" :question/problem "Consider the vector space ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$ of all $2\\times 2$ matrices over $R,$ and its subset $E$ containing all diagonal $2\\times 2$ matrices.\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $E$ is closed under matrix addition\n- $E$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n- $E$ is a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$\n- $E$ is **not** a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. If ${A}_{1}$ and ${A}_{2}$ are two matrices from $E,$ then \n\n$$\n{A}_{1}+{A}_{2}\n$$\n\n is a diagonal matrix. This matrix belongs to $E.$ So, $E$ is closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $A$ is an element of $E,$ and $k\\in R,$ then \n\n$$\nkA\n$$\n\n is a diagonal matrix. This matrix belongs to $E.$ So, $E$ is closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is true, while statement IV is false. $E$ is a subspace because it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186350728 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8f306cf2-6881-5948-90bd-4e0ce98b4116" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subspaces of Matrix Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43d92592-033e-5dc9-aa2c-5ac26a141904" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350730} {:answer/id #uuid "638c7ec3-b137-5cf5-b0cf-2d76fd8240df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350731} {:answer/id #uuid "7d1e1c1e-e963-5fc7-82dd-13e6786d172c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350732} {:answer/id #uuid "c3f2dbc5-c09b-5ff1-b43a-4a47a4e71306" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350733} {:answer/id #uuid "c79356eb-54eb-5ef6-9a22-fd7e950a57eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350734}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7d1e1c1e-e963-5fc7-82dd-13e6786d172c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350732} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8ce4ca7-0c9f-50d7-9058-0854dfe3ad80" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350729}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f6d2e36e-f98a-5232-ba28-02ba4b8a6484" :question/math-academy-id "q-94629" :question/problem "Consider the vector space ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$ of all $2\\times 2$ matrices over $R$ and its subset $F={A\\in {\\text{M}}_{2}(R)\\,|\\,[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]A=A[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]}.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $F$ is closed under matrix addition\n- $F$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n- $F$ is a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$\n- $F$ is **not** a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. If ${A}_{1}$ and ${A}_{2}$ are two matrices from $F,$ then ${A}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]{A}_{1}$ and ${A}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]{A}_{2}.$ So, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({A}_{1}+{A}_{2})[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}] & ={A}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]+{A}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]{A}_{1}+[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]{A}_{2} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]({A}_{1}+{A}_{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${A}_{1}+{A}_{2}$ is a matrix from $F.$ So, $F$ is closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $A$ is an element of $F,$ then $A[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]A.$ For $k\\in R,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(kA)[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}] & =k\\cdot A[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =k[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]A \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}](kA).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $kA$ is a matrix from $F.$ So, $F$ is closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is true, while statement IV is false. $F$ is a subspace because it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186350735 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8f306cf2-6881-5948-90bd-4e0ce98b4116" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subspaces of Matrix Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2708ddf5-06f6-546e-afba-c49565f9fdd4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350737} {:answer/id #uuid "c4478e1e-e773-5ff9-875c-9ed499835d7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350738} {:answer/id #uuid "140e46e0-21b0-5d9f-954d-3f554622d179" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350739} {:answer/id #uuid "67361646-174e-5340-b1ce-e24fa0a1735a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350740} {:answer/id #uuid "857a864a-a246-56e2-80d9-ba304020a137" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350741}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "857a864a-a246-56e2-80d9-ba304020a137" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350741} :answer-field/id #uuid "21d3a40c-4e52-5bbe-9c7e-ae124c2f2a68" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350736}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bc4f94c2-8647-5894-9126-c937860312fd" :question/math-academy-id "q-94631" :question/problem "Consider the vector space ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$ of all $2\\times 2$ matrices over $R$ and its subset $H={[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]}.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $H$ is closed under matrix addition\n- $H$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n- $H$ is a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$\n- $H$ is **not** a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. For example, if ${A}_{1}={A}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}],$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1}+{A}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is not a matrix from $H.$ So, $H$ is *not* closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is false. For example, if $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]$ and $k=2,$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}kA & =2[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is not a matrix from $H.$ So, $H$ is *not* closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is false, while statement IV is true. $H$ is a *not* subspace because it's not closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"IV only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186350742 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef65513d-1e9e-571f-8b93-4e2d63aed68e" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subspaces of Function Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a0c74a5f-b58f-5929-9579-48df8a7b4af9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350744} {:answer/id #uuid "f3e7ca52-8deb-57c7-82fb-0096c905db96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350745} {:answer/id #uuid "2cf826a9-3e6f-5c25-a17d-07e9b4de2394" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350746} {:answer/id #uuid "479ae802-368f-5745-ab33-080d1d96351f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350747} {:answer/id #uuid "097fe3c3-adf8-58ec-ab92-bf0d76267c13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350748}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "097fe3c3-adf8-58ec-ab92-bf0d76267c13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350748} :answer-field/id #uuid "54274b23-7dcf-51bc-a83b-714784cb5b83" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350743}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "fc18f1a0-e2bd-52ed-93fe-4648ff2e2097" :question/math-academy-id "q-94633" :question/problem "Consider the vector space $C[0,1]$ of all continuous functions $f:[0,1]\\to R$ and its subset $Q$ containing all polynomials of degree exactly $2.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $Q$ is closed under function addition\n- $Q$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n- $Q$ is a subspace of $C[0,1]$\n- $Q$ is **not** a subspace of $C[0,1]$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. For example, if $f(x)={x}^{2}$ and $g(x)=-{x}^{2},$ then\n\n$$\nf(x)+g(x)={x}^{2}+(-{x}^{2})=0.\n$$\n\nSo, $Q$ is *not* closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is false. For example, if $f(x)={x}^{2}$ and $k=0,$ then\n\n$$\nkf(x)=0\\cdot {x}^{2}=0.\n$$\n\n \nSo, $Q$ is *not* closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is false, while statement IV is true. $Q$ is *not* a subspace because it's not closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"IV only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186350749 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef65513d-1e9e-571f-8b93-4e2d63aed68e" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subspaces of Function Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "59ca04ee-2415-550c-bba3-fbcc6b9c8730" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350751} {:answer/id #uuid "45eaf453-7518-5464-8324-afe3488e8f92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350752} {:answer/id #uuid "698dbec1-f11e-5e91-b522-83c17b4ce688" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350753} {:answer/id #uuid "01e9b045-587f-5ad2-a768-1bb1f7b868d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350754} {:answer/id #uuid "9d9a052f-d7b6-55ad-9a2a-4ab6b0a9091b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350755}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "698dbec1-f11e-5e91-b522-83c17b4ce688" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350753} :answer-field/id #uuid "347c020d-2c38-583d-90ea-b7a0303fd146" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350750}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "10bf265e-e38c-58b3-b176-163baf65aeab" :question/math-academy-id "q-94642" :question/problem "Consider the vector space $C[-2,2]$ of all continuous functions $f:[-2,2]\\to R$ and its subset $E$ containing all even functions.\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $E$ is closed under function addition\n- $E$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n- $E$ is a subspace of $C[-2,2]$\n- $E$ is **not** a subspace of $C[-2,2]$\n\n*Hint: $f$ is even if $f(-x)=f(x)$ for all $x\\in [-2,2].$*" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. If $f(x),g(x)\\in E,$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f+g)(-x) & =f(-x)+g(-x) \\\\  & =f(x)+g(x) \\\\  & =(f+g)(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $E$ is closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $f(x)\\in E$ and $k\\in R,$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(kf)(-x) & =kf(-x) \\\\  & =kf(x) \\\\  & =(kf)(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $E$ is closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is true, while statement IV is false. $E$ is a subspace because it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III only.\""}]}
